```text
FINANCE COMMIflEE
MINUTES
Due to the Martin Luther King Jr. holiday, a meeting of the Finance Committee was instead held
on Wednesday, January 21,2026, in City Council Chambers and via electronic meeting, starting
at 12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS:
Ken Esquibel, Chairman; Dr. Kathy Emmons (via Zoom); Jeff
White; and Lawrence Wolfe. Absent: Mark Moody.
AGENDA ITEMS
8.
APPLICATION/LICENSES/PERMITS:
b)
Application for a transfer of ownership of retail liquor license filed with the City
Clerk’s Office for Ace’s Range LLC d/b/a Ace’s Range, 1505 Pioneer Ave.,
Cheyenne, WY (license currently held by F & G Corporation d/b/a The Green
Door).
Mr. White moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Wolfe. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Kylie Soden, City Clerk, provided a staffreport. Ben Trautwein, current license holder, and April
Brimmer Kunz and J Brent Kunz, applicant, provided additional information.
Committee
members Emmons, White, and Wolfe commented on the item.
c)
Application for a transfer of ownership of retail liquor license filed with the City
Clerk’s Office for Westby Edge LLC d/b/a Westby Edge Brewing, 714 W. 20th St.,
Cheyenne, WY (license currently held by Scooters Scoreboard Inc.).
Mr. White moved to approve, seconded by Mr. Wolfe. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Kylie Soden, City Clerk, provWed a staffreport and noted that due to the timely nature ofthe two
years in-operational status under the current owner expiring before the next regularly scheduled
meeting ofthe governing body, a Special Meeting ofthe will be held on Friday, January 23,2026,
at 12:00 p.m. for its final consideration. Darrin Westby, applicant, provided a brief history of
Westhy Edge Brewing.
Chairman Esquibel and committee member Wolfe commented on the
item.
16.
RESOLUTION
— Re-appropriating the Fiscal Year 2026 Budget of the City of Cheyenne
According to the Provisions of W.S. fi 16-4-112 & 16-4-113. (SPONSOR
— MR.
ESQUIBEL)
Mr. White moved to adopt, seconded by Mr. Wolfe. Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
```

