```text
Mr. White moved to accept the bid from Hypertec USA Inc. in an amount not to exceed
$239,577.88, seconded by Mr. Wolfe, Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Dustin Swalla. Assistant Director Information Technology, provided a staff report and committee
member Wolfe commented on the item.
OTHER ITEMS FOR TIlE AGENDA:
RESOLUTION
- Authorizing the submission of an application by the City of Cheyenne for state
funding through the Office of State Lands and Investments for Rodeo Grounds Pedestrian
Transportation Infrastructure Grant, and authorizing the execution and submittal of all necessary
documents in support of the application. (SPONSOR
— MR. ESQUIBEL)
Mr. White moved to adopt, seconded by Dr. Emmons, Motion carried by unanimous voice vote.
Amber Ash, Mayor’s Chief of Staff, provided a staff report and Tom Cobb, City Engineer,
provided information related to the design of the proposed pedestrian bridge.
Mary Kay Hill,
Cheyenne Frontier Days Board of Directors member, provided additional information related to
the partnership between multiple entities. Committee members Emmons, White, and Wolfe
commented on the item.
There being no further items for the agenda to come before the Finance Committee, the meeting
was adjourned at 12:54 p.m.
Submitted by,
Jennifer McClelland
Executive Assistant to the City Council
